; ted-detoka5-without-tokenise (#354): Block Save writes the middle lines
; of a block through detoka5 even without tokenising, so a Latin-1
; character and the byte behind it become a token name.  TED alone (no
; token list: tokenise off; under blitz2 TED tokenises, and tokit clears
; bit 7 of the text), lines "a", "; Größe", "b", "c"; block from the start
; of line 1 (F1) to the end of line 3 (BOTTOM, F2 at the start of line 4),
; Block Save.  Correct: the three lines as they are; the original writes a
; token name for ö and ß.
; @file bo.bas "a\n; Gr\xf6\xdfe\nb\nc"
; @source F bo.bas
; @command blitz2:ted @FILE@
; @expect data blk.txt "a\n; Gr\xf6\xdfe\nb\n"
timeout 10
wait screen
key 50
menu 2 1
key 51
menu 1 2
wait freq "Name to save block as"
freq ok "TEDRUN:work/blk.txt"
wait screen
menu 0 9
wait exit
